cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Vesuvius AutoResearch (bountyhunter)"
abstract: >-
  An autonomous, evidence-gated research loop for 3D ink detection on the
  Vesuvius Challenge: it samples tweaks to a training configuration (losses,
  augmentations, optimisation; the architecture is pinned), trains each
  candidate under a fixed budget, scores it on a held-out validation fragment,
  and keeps it only if its threshold-swept F1 beats the incumbent's, gated by
  AP-prevalence lift. All ML outputs use a 64x64 window within the Challenge's
  hallucination-mitigation cap.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Marrs
    given-names: Jon
repository-code: "https://github.com/jonmarrs/vesuvius-autoresearch"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-03-23"
keywords:
